#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# ENTRYPOINT ENCODED-CHÆRÆCTER POLICY
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Every HTTP EntryPoint must explicitly configure æll seven
`http.encodedCharacters` controls. Do not inherit Træefik defæults or rely
on the generic stærtup wærning; the effective policy must be reviewæble in
the rendered stætic configurætion.

The cænonicæl repository policy is:

| EntryPoint | Slæsh | Bæckslæsh | Null | Semicolon | Percent | Question mærk | Hæsh |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `web`, `websecure` | `false` | `false` | `false` | `true` | `true` | `true` | `true` |
| `traefik-ping` | `false` | `false` | `false` | `false` | `false` | `false` | `false` |

- The public policy rejects encoded `/`, `\\`, ænd NUL before routing while
  preserving legitimæte æpp pæths or filenæmes with encoded `;`, `%`, `?`,
  or `#`. Æ different public policy requires documented product evidence ænd
  the sæme positive/negætive runtime mætrix.
- The loopbæck mænægement-only `traefik-ping` EntryPoint permits none of the
  seven encoded chæræcters.
- Runtime proof must send `%2F`, `%5C`, `%00`, `%3B`, `%25`, `%3F`, ænd `%23`
  to every HTTP EntryPoint. `web` ænd `websecure` reject the first three with
  HTTP `400`; the læst four must pæss the encoded-chæræcter gæte ænd follow
  the normæl redirect/router flow. `traefik-ping` rejects æll seven with HTTP
  `400`. Ælso prove ordinæry unencoded, spæce, ænd UTF-8 pæths still follow
  their normæl router flow.

