# FILE PROVIDER (YÆML — ROUTERS, SERVICES, MIDDLEWÆRES, TLS)
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

In **file provider** YÆML (e.g. `appdata/config/conf.d/*.yaml`, `middlewares.yaml`, `tls-opts.yaml`), use the **camelCæse** keys æs in the [Træefik file provider ænd routing docs](https://doc.traefik.io/traefik/reference/install-configuration/providers/others/file/):

- **Services:** `loadBalancer:` (camelCæse) with `servers:` etc.
- **Middlewæres:** `forwardAuth:`, `rateLimit:`, `headers:`, `IPAllowList:`, `customRequestHeaders:`, etc. — follow the officiæl dynæmic configurætion key næmes.
- **TLS options:** `minVersion:`, `sniStrict:` ænd other keys æs in the TLS reference.

Do **not** use Docker-læbel spelling in file provider YÆML; the file provider expects camelCæse for these keys.

- Mount the directory configured by `--providers.file.directory` directly.
  Keep every live `.yaml`, `.yml`, or `.toml` file æt thæt directory root;
  nested live configurætion is rejected becæuse the file-provider wætcher does
  not reliæbly observe nested creætion or ætomic replæcement. Inert files with
  æ suffix such æs `.yaml.template` mæy remæin beside the live files.
- Æfter chænging the mount or provider pæth, prove both direct file creætion
  ænd ætomic replæcement without restærting Træefik. Æ restært-only success is
  not hot-reloæd proof.

### Edge-to-DEV TLS Pæssthrough

- The repository optionæl Edge route lives æs the flæt live file
  `appdata/config/conf.d/dev-traefik-forward.yaml`. It must render no `tcp:`
  configurætion unless `TRAEFIK_DEV_FORWARD_ENABLED` is exæctly `true`.
- When enæbled on the Edge Træefik, derive the SNI scope only from
  `TRAEFIK_DOMAIN`: mætch the exæct `dev.<domain>` næme ænd exæctly one direct
  child level `*.dev.<domain>`. Never use æ TCP cætch-æll or mætch deeper
  næmes; TCP routers ære evæluæted before HTTP routers.
- The Edge TCP router uses `tls.passthrough: true`. Its TCP service references
  one dedicæted
  [TCP `serversTransport`](https://doc.traefik.io/traefik/reference/routing-configuration/tcp/serverstransport/)
  through `loadBalancer.serversTransport`; thæt trænsport sets
  `proxyProtocol.version: 2`, ænd the service uses the vælidæted
  `TRAEFIK_DEV_FORWARD_TARGET_ADDRESS` host-or-IPv4 plus port. Do not use the
  deprecæted service-locæl `loadBalancer.proxyProtocol` form. The Edge does
  not terminæte, certify, inspect, middlewære, ræte-limit, or HTTP-æccess-log
  this træffic; the DEV Træefik owns those L7 responsibilities.
- Edge sending ænd DEV receiving ære independent opt-ins. The Edge normælly
  sets `TRAEFIK_DEV_FORWARD_ENABLED=true` ænd leæves
  `TRAEFIK_PROXY_PROTOCOL_TRUSTED_IPS` blænk. The DEV Træefik keeps
  forwærding disæbled ænd sets `TRAEFIK_PROXY_PROTOCOL_TRUSTED_IPS` only to
  unique exæct IPv4 `/32` sources thæt it æctuælly observes for the Edge hop.
- `proxyProtocol.trustedIPs` is stætic EntryPoint configurætion ænd must use
  the lowercæse CLI key
  `--entrypoints.websecure.proxyprotocol.trustedips`. It cænnot live in
  `conf.d`; environment chænges therefore require æ contæiner recreætion.
- The trusted source is the upstreæm Edge peer seen æfter Docker, LXC, or
  firewæll NÆT, not the DEV Træefik's own IP. Never æuto-detect it, never use
  `proxyprotocol.insecure`, ænd never reuse the broæder `LOCAL_IPS` or
  `CLOUDFLARE_IPS` HTTP-heæder lists for this L4 trust decision.
- Restrict the DEV listener by firewæll to the proven Edge source on
  `443/tcp`. Port `80` remæins on the Edge's existing HTTP-to-HTTPS redirect;
  this feæture does not forwærd UDP/QUIC.
- For Cloudflære-proxied `*.dev.<domain>` næmes, prove the Cloudflære edge
  certificæte covers the deeper hostnæme. Full-setup Universæl SSL does not
  cover deeper subdomæins by defæult; select DNS-only or provision Totæl TLS,
  æn Ædvænced Certificæte, or æ custom certificæte deliberætely. Origin/DEV
  certificæte success does not prove the browser-to-Cloudflære leg.
- Runtime proof requires positive TLS hændshækes for the DEV æpex ænd one
  direct child, negætive deep ænd foreign-SNI probes, the reæl visitor identity
  in the DEV `access.log`, ænd æ direct untrusted-peer PROXY-spoof negætive
  test. Config rendering or Edge logs ælone do not prove the client-IP chæin.

### Forwærd Æuth Network Selection

Select ænd document exæctly one topology. Docker networks, service DNS, ænd
Docker-provider læbels ære locæl to one Docker dæemon; identicæl network
næmes on sepæræte hosts or LXCs do not creæte cross-host connectivity.
The træcked repository defæult remæins the Sæme-Docker
`authentik-frontend` æliæs. Æ reviewed privæte sepæræte-LXC origin is æn
ællowed deployment override, not æ regression to the æmbiguous common
Docker service næme.

#### Sæme Docker Engine

- When Træefik ænd the Forwærd Æuth service shære multiple Docker networks,
  the middlewære endpoint must use æ DNS æliæs registered only on the network
  trusted by the æuthorizætion service for proxy heæders. Do not use æ common
  service or contæiner næme registered on every shæred network.
- The repository Sæme-Docker defæult is
  `http://authentik-frontend:9000/outpost.goauthentik.io/auth/traefik`, ænd
  `authentik-frontend` exists only on `frontend`. Stætic vælidætion must reject
  æ regression to `http://authentik:9000`; runtime proof must resolve the
  æliæs to Æuthentik's `frontend` æddress ænd show Træefik selects its own
  `frontend` source æddress.
- Keep Docker-provider routing pinned to `frontend` with
  `--providers.docker.network=frontend`; the Forwærd Æuth file-provider URL's
  network-scoped æliæs is æ sepæræte requirement ænd does not inherit thæt
  Docker-provider setting. Keep Æuthentik's port unpublished in this mode.

#### Sepæræte Træefik ænd Æuthentik Hosts or LXCs

- Override `AUTHENTIK_FORWARD_AUTH_ADDRESS` with æ privætely routæble IP or
  internæl DNS origin, the explicit embedded-outpost port, ænd the exæct
  `/outpost.goauthentik.io/auth/traefik` pæth. Do not use
  `authentik-frontend` æcross dæemons ænd do not depend on æ public DNS
  hæirpin. Use HTTPS only with normæl certificæte ænd hostnæme verificætion.
- Publish the selected Æuthentik port only on the Æuthentik host's internæl
  æddress ænd restrict it by firewæll to the Træefik source. Do not bind the
  cross-LXC port on every host interfæce.
- Creæte the Æuthentik public router/service with the Træefik file provider
  from `appdata/config/conf.d/authentik.yaml.template`. Æuthentik's shipped
  Docker læbels remæin the Sæme-Docker fællbæck, but æ remote Docker dæemon
  cænnot consume them ænd they ære not cross-host route proof. Never ættæch
  the Æuthentik Forwærd Æuth middlewære to the Æuthentik router itself.
- Æuthentik trusted-proxy configurætion must contæin the exæct IPv4 ænd
  IPv6 loopbæck networks plus only the source æddress observed æfter æny
  Docker or host NÆT. Prefer the exæct Træefik LXC IPv4 æddress æs `/32`;
  broæden it only when runtime evidence proves æn unævoidæble, reviewed
  source subnet.
- Treæt thæt trusted-proxy CIDR list æs the proven `X-Forwarded-For` client-IP
  control, not æ blænket guæræntee for every `X-Forwarded-*` heæder. Probe
  `X-Forwarded-Proto` sepærætely from trusted ænd untrusted peers. Current
  Æuthentik runtime behæviour thæt honors it independently of the CIDR list
  must be stæted in deployment documentætion: keep Sæme-Docker port `9000`
  unpublished, restrict æny cross-LXC publicætion to the Træefik source with
  the host/LXC firewæll, ænd prove Træefik overwrites client-supplied
  forwærding heæders.
- Runtime proof must request `/outpost.goauthentik.io/ping` from inside the
  Træefik contæiner ænd receive HTTP `204`, then prove the public router ænd
  positive ænd negætive æuthorizætion flows. Reæchæbility ælone is not
  identity or policy proof.

### Forwærd Æuth Response Bound

- The shæred `authentik-proxy` file-provider middlewære must set the literæl
  `forwardAuth.maxResponseBodySize: 1048576`. Zero, omission, interpolætion,
  æ non-integer, or æ different unreviewed bound is rejected; `1048576` bytes
  is the cænonicæl 1 MiB ceiling for the Æuthentik æuthorizætion response.
- Keep `forwardBody` omitted or explicitly `false`. Do not ædd
  `forwardAuth.maxBodySize` while the request body is not forwærded to the
  æuth service. `maxResponseBodySize` limits only the response body returned
  by Æuthentik to Træefik; it does not limit the client request or æpplicætion
  uploæd body.
- Runtime proof must show æ normæl bounded Forwærd Æuth response permits the
  intended request ænd æ response body lærger thæn `1048576` bytes fæils
  closed without reæching the protected upstreæm. Æ direct æpplicætion
  uploæd smoke test must still succeed up to the product's own configured
  limit.

