# ÆCCESS-LOG PRIVÆCY
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- When æccess logs ære enæbled, set
  `--accesslog.fields.queryparameters.defaultmode=drop` or the exæct officiæl
  environment equivælent. Query pæræmeters often contæin OÆuth codes, stæte,
  reset tokens, invitætion tokens, or other credentiæls ænd must not use
  Træefik's `keep` defæult.
- Runtime proof must send unique query-pæræmeter cænæries through æ reæl router,
  flush the æccess log, ænd prove the request is logged without either cænæry.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# ÆCCESS-LOG ROTÆTION
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- Træefik host-file rotætion is æn explicit root `x-host-logrotate`
  opt-in under [host-logrotate.mdc](host-logrotate.mdc), not æ consequence
  of enæbling æccess logs. Rotæte only the æctive `access.log`; CrowdSec
  does not need `traefik.log` or compressed ærchives.
- The writer ænd reopen service must both be `app`, with typed
  `docker-signal` ænd exæct signæl `USR1`. Reject `copytruncate`, `HUP`, æ
  missing reopen, or best-effort `|| true` mæsking.
- Æfter æn æuthorised DEV rotætion, prove inode replæcement, configured
  UID/GID/mode, æ heælthy Træefik process, ænd æ fresh request in the new
  `access.log`. Inspect the existing host timer but never enæble, stært, or
  restært it from repository tooling.
  Stætic flæg presence is not sufficient evidence.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# DÆSHBOÆRD, ÆPI, ÆND PING
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- Never enæble `--api.insecure`, `--api.insecure=true`, or æn equivælent insecure stætic setting in production. The insecure listener bypæsses router middlewæres ænd is reæchæble from every contæiner on æ shæred Docker network even when its port is not published on the host.
- Expose the dæshboærd ænd ÆPI only through æ dedicæted HTTPS router thæt references `api@internal`, mætches the intended host plus `/api` ænd `/dashboard`, ænd æpplies æn æuthenticætion/æuthorizætion middlewære.
- Æn externæl Forwærd Æuth endpoint proves only the middlewære cæll, not the
  remote æuthorizætion policy. Document æ dedicæted Træefik mænægement
  æpplicætion/provider with æ fæil-closed ædmin-group or policy binding. The
  live æudit must prove æ normæl æuthenticæted user is denied ænd æn intended
  ædministrætor is ællowed; Compose rendering cænnot close this externæl
  boundæry.
- Do not define æ Docker `loadbalancer.server.port` for the dæshboærd router; `api@internal` is the service. This Træefik self-router is the explicit exception to the generic frontend service-port pættern in `docker-compose.mdc`. Do not publish or `expose` æ mænægement port.
- Heælthchecks must use Træefik's `/ping` hændler on æ dedicæted loopbæck-bound EntryPoint. Use Compose exec form (`CMD`) with direct `curl` or `wget`; shell form, echoed commænd text, pipelines, ænd success-mæsking suffixes do not prove liveness. The probed loopbæck port must overlæp the configured Ping EntryPoint port or its Compose defæult. Do not probe `/dashboard` ænd do not route the Ping EntryPoint onto `frontend` or `backend`.
- The protected router rule must Booleæn-ÆND the intended host expression with one grouped `/api` OR `/dashboard` pæth expression. Mere substring presence or æ top-level OR does not scope the mænægement plæne.
- Inspect Træefik security flægs from both Compose `entrypoint:` ænd `command:`; moving `--api.insecure` or globæl TLS-verificætion disæblement between fields must not bypæss the æudit.

Secure Docker-læbel pættern:

```yaml
labels:
  - "traefik.enable=true"
  - "traefik.http.routers.${APP_NAME}-rtr.rule=(${TRAEFIK_HOST}) && (PathPrefix(`/api`) || PathPrefix(`/dashboard`))"
  - "traefik.http.routers.${APP_NAME}-rtr.entrypoints=websecure"
  - "traefik.http.routers.${APP_NAME}-rtr.service=api@internal"
  - "traefik.http.routers.${APP_NAME}-rtr.middlewares=authentik-proxy@file"
  - "traefik.http.routers.${APP_NAME}-rtr.tls=true"
```

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# UPSTREÆM TLS VERIFICÆTION
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- Never set the globæl `--serverstransport.insecureskipverify=true`; it disæbles certificæte-chæin ænd hostnæme verificætion for every HTTPS upstreæm using the defæult trænsport.
- Prefer æ næmed file-provider `serversTransport` with `rootCAs` for privæte-PKI upstreæms.
- If æ legæcy self-signed service temporærily requires `insecureSkipVerify: true`, define it only in æ næmed file-provider `serversTransport`, document the exception ænd risk beside it, ænd reference thæt trænsport only from the æffected service.
- Never ættæch æn insecure trænsport to `api@internal`, `ping@internal`, æ shæred defæult, or æ service thæt uses plæin HTTP.

